lly preserves red cell mass", "Metabolic/genetic disorder: Unlikely given adult age and localized hematologic findings (no multisystem involvement)", "Vitamin deficiency syndrome: Possible but contradicted by normal serum calcium and absence of malabsorption evidence", "Autoimmune pancytopenia: Considered but ranked lower due to absence of typical autoimmune markers (e.g., antinuclear antibodies, complement abnormalities)"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional B-symptoms (weight loss, night sweats, fever)", "Significant pancytopenia with blasts on peripheral smear"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.0, "danger": 0.85, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.8284530022203606, "posterior": 0.8284530022203606, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["chronic myeloid leukemia", "polycythemia vera", "essential thrombocythemia", "primary myelofibrosis"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.007, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.021, "danger": 0.75, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.10543768119105126, "posterior": 0.10543768119105126, "danger": 0.3, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.3, "interrupt_relevance": 0.4, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}}, "frontier": ["B2", "B5"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Is the high leukocyte count (57,500/mm³) in a subacute phase supportive of Essential Thrombocythemia in accelerated phase despite thrombocytopenia (platelets 109,000/mm³)?", "summary": "Thrombocytopenia (platelets 109,000/mm³) argues against ET in accelerated phase, which typically presents with elevated platelets. The subacute phase is not definitive for ET."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the mild ataxia and visual symptoms suggest extramedullary complications of Primary Myelofibrosis in accelerated phase, despite the absence of splenomegaly or fibrosis findings on exam?", "summary": "Absence of splenomegaly and marrow fibrosis on exam weakens PMF in accelerated phase. Extramedullary symptoms are less typical for this phase."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of known CML history and splenomegaly in a patient with subacute onset (days) and visual symptoms argue against CML in blast crisis as the primary diagnosis?", "summary": "No prior CML history and lack of splenomegaly are strong evidence against CML in blast crisis, which typically has a known chronic phase and splenomegaly."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the anemia (Hb 10g/dL) contradict the typical presentation of Polycythemia Vera in blast phase, which preserves red cell mass, and reduce the posterior of PV in accelerated phase?", "summary": "Anemia (Hb 10g/dL) is inconsistent with PV in blast phase, which preserves red cell mass. This weakens PV in accelerated phase as a primary diagnosis."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the thrombocytopenia (platelets 109,000/mm³) argue against Essential Thrombocythemia in accelerated phase, which typically presents with elevated platelets rather than reduced counts?", "summary": "Thrombocytopenia (platelets 109,000/mm³) is inconsistent with ET in accelerated phase, which typically presents with elevated platelets."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of splenomegaly or marrow fibrosis findings on physical exam argue against Primary Myelofibrosis in accelerated phase as the diagnosis despite pancytopenia?", "summary": "PMF in accelerated phase typically features splenomegaly and marrow fibrosis. Their absence on exam weakens this diagnosis."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B2", 0.221], ["B2.2", 0.118], ["B5", 0.089]]}, {"top": [["B2", 0.79], ["B2.1", 0.474], ["B2.2", 0.158]]}, {"top": [["B2", 0.43], ["B2.1", 0.258], ["B5", 0.102]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "No immediate life-threatening instability markers present", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading terminal branch posterior (0.258) remains below 0.75 threshold. Dangerous alternatives B2.1 (CML blast crisis) and B2.2 (PV accelerated phase) remain unresolved with distinct management implications (BCR-ABL1 testing vs. JAK2 mutation analysis). Tree depth (2) is below max_tree_depth (3). Critical discriminators like bone marrow biopsy for fibrosis or cytogenetics have not been requested."}, "turn_budget_used": 4, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.9, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.25815875884139755, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Acute lymphoblastic leukemia"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Acute myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Chronic lymphocytic leukemia"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Chronic myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Multiple myeloma"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'Myelofibrosis', 'Pancytopenia', 'Pansynostosis', 'Splenomegaly', 'Increased circulating myelocyte count'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "tool_use_log": [], "root_revision_needed": false, "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B2", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.581}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B5", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "posterior": 0.105, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 0, "disconfirming": 0, "last_disconfirming_digest": ""}, "action_intents": [{"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}], "considered_alternatives": []}, "discriminator_hints": "[Knowledge Layer: coverage=33%, source=primekg]\n\nRelated to Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts: hematopoietic and lymphoid cell neoplasm, lymphoid leukemia (disease), lymphoma\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  and night sweats → pain → Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts\n  and night sweats → fatigue → Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts"}
